>>
Rule 1 (input must be at least 2-D: matrices or batches of matrices)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 2 (explicitly exclude 1-D tensors)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∨ ndim(v_1) > 2
>>
Rule 3 (all existing dimensions are valid sizes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (explicitly disallow 1-D input)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≠ 1
>>
Rule 6 (the last two dimensions exist and have valid sizes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ∀k ∈ [ndim(v_1) - 2, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, k) ≥ 0
